exports[`export ZIP > documents (snapshot) > ASSEMBLY.md 1`] = `
"# stacklamp — assembly

Configuration: https://jahoefne.github.io/stacklamp/#v=1

## Hardware

- **Core:** 1500 mm aluminium tube Ø 20 mm, no cut needed.
- **3 × M4 screws** (8–10 mm set screws or self-tapping screws) for the collar holes (Ø 3.3 mm), or a few dots of hot glue instead.
- **Weight plate** Ø 155 × 25 mm with a 30 mm bore (a standard cast-iron dumbbell plate); it sits in the base's 158 × 26 mm underside pocket and keeps the lamp from tipping.
- **LED strip**, 10 mm wide, 12 V or 24 V, wrapped around the rod between 78 mm and 1515.5 mm above the floor (1437.5 mm). Length estimate:

| Wrap | Strip length |
|---|---|
| tight helix (pitch 10 mm) | ≈ 10.5 m |
| open helix (pitch 20 mm) | ≈ 5.4 m |
| open helix (pitch 40 mm) | ≈ 3 m |
| one straight run | ≈ 1.44 m |

- **Power supply:** a certified 12 V or 24 V (SELV) supply matching the strip, rated for the strip power (W/m × length) plus 20 %, with an inline switch or dimmer. The supply stays outside the lamp.
- **Printed parts:** base, 11 × inner segment, 11 × outer segment, top cover (see PRINT-PLAN.md).

## Steps

1. Press the weight plate into the pocket on the underside of the base. If it rattles, a few dots of hot glue or a strip of tape hold it.
2. Push the rod into the collar until it stands on the socket floor, 15 mm below the base top. Tighten the 3 screws (27.75 mm above the base top) evenly so the rod stands upright.
3. Wrap the LED strip around the rod from the collar top (78 mm) up to 1515.5 mm, where the cover boss begins: the top 12.5 mm of the rod slide into the boss and stay bare. Secure both ends.
4. Route the strip's lead down the Ø 8 mm hole beside the collar into the tunnel and out of the base rim. Connect it to the power supply outside the lamp.
5. Stack the 11 inner segments onto the inner ring of the base, foot (socket) down, in the colour order of PRINT-PLAN.md (band 1 at the bottom). Each foot slides over the rim below and sits on its 45° shoulder.
6. Stack the 11 outer segments onto the outer ring the same way.
7. Fit the cover: the boss goes over the rod end, the inner ring over the top inner segment, the outer ring over the top outer segment, whose rim bears on the cover plate. The rod ends 2.5 mm below the boss hole ceiling and the inner stack 2.2 mm below the plate.

## Safety

- Use **only SELV LED strips (12 V or 24 V)** with a certified, correctly rated power supply. Never bring mains voltage into the lamp.
- **PETG softens at about 80 °C.** Keep the air intakes in the base and the slits in the cover open so warm air can rise through the stacks; use moderate strip power (the aluminium rod works as a heat sink) and check after an hour that no part gets hot to the touch.
- **Anchor the lamp against tipping.** It is 1.53 m tall on a 240 mm base: always use the weight plate, stand it on a level floor and keep it out of reach of small children and pets.
- The printed parts are not a structural load path: do not lift the lamp by the cover or the segments.
"
`;

