"# stacklamp — print plan

Generated 2026-10-22T12:00:00.000Z by stacklamp 0.1.0.
Reopen this lamp: https://jahoefne.github.io/stacklamp/#v=1

## Summary

| Item | Value |
|---|---|
| Rod | 1500 mm aluminium tube Ø 20 mm, no cut needed |
| Lamp height | 1533.5 mm (base 43 mm + stacks + 3 mm cover plate) |
| Outer stack | 11 × 154.5 mm segments, Ø 200 mm, pitch 133.25 mm (+3.0 % from the 150 mm target) |
| Inner stack | 11 × 154.3 mm segments, Ø 60 mm, pitch 133.05 mm (+2.9 % from the 150 mm target) |
| Height mode | auto (segment heights fitted to the rod) |
| Joint | 20 mm overlap, 0.25 mm clearance, seat height 21.25 mm |
| Rod end | 2.5 mm below the cover's boss hole ceiling |
| Inner stack top | 2.2 mm below the cover plate |

## Printer fit — Bambu Lab P1S / X1C / A1, 256 × 256 × 250 mm

| Part | Size (mm) | Fits bed | Fits height |
|---|---|---|---|
| Base | 240 × 240 × 78 | yes | yes |
| Inner segment | 62.1 × 62.1 × 154.3 | yes | yes |
| Outer segment | 202.1 × 202.1 × 154.5 | yes | yes |
| Top cover | 205.3 × 205.3 × 23 | yes | yes |

## Parts

| File | Part | Copies | Colours | Triangles | Volume each (cm³) | Solid each (g) | Estimate each (g) | Estimate total (g) |
|---|---|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| base.3mf | Base | 1 | any (opaque recommended) | 53,950 | 1488.2 | 1890.0 | 733.2 | 733 |
| inner-segment.3mf | Inner segment | 11 | Clear × 6, Amber × 5 | 4,000 | 23.1 | 29.3 | 26.9 | 296 |
| outer-segment.3mf | Outer segment | 11 | Amber × 4, Teal × 4, Clear × 3 | 12,800 | 77.5 | 98.4 | 90.5 | 995 |
| top-cover.3mf | Top cover | 1 | any (opaque recommended) | 33,408 | 131.1 | 166.5 | 125.5 | 125 |

Total ≈ 2150 g / 704 m of 1.75 mm PETG (density 1.27 g/cm³). The estimates are what the slicer extrudes with the settings below: vase lines with rounded flanks for the segments, walls + 20 % infill for the base and cover; the base includes ≈ 52 g of tree supports.

### Filament per colour

| Colour | Inner segments | Outer segments | Mass (g) | Filament (m) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Clear (#e8eef0) | 6 | 3 | 433 | 141.7 |
| Amber (#f0a020) | 5 | 4 | 496 | 162.5 |
| Teal (#109090) | 0 | 4 | 362 | 118.4 |

### Colour order (bottom → top)

**Outer stack**  
1. Amber  
2. Teal  
3. Clear  
4. Amber  
5. Teal  
6. Clear  
7. Amber  
8. Teal  
9. Clear  
10. Amber  
11. Teal

**Inner stack**  
1. Clear  
2. Amber  
3. Clear  
4. Amber  
5. Clear  
6. Amber  
7. Clear  
8. Amber  
9. Clear  
10. Amber  
11. Clear

Slicers ignore the colours stored in the 3MF files (they are a viewer hint only): load the filament for each print yourself.

## Slicer settings

- All parts: 0.6 mm nozzle, PETG at 240–250 °C, bed 70–80 °C on the **Textured PEI plate** (Bambu Studio's Generic PETG profile has no Cool Plate temperature).
- One object per plate, left where the file places it (centred on the bed).

### Segments — spiral vase

- Line width = wall = 0.8 mm: in Bambu Studio set Quality → Line width → **Outer wall** and **First layer** to 0.8 mm.
- Spiral vase mode on: 1 wall, 0 top and 0 bottom layers, 0 % infill.
- Layer height 0.3 mm, part cooling fan 30–50 %.
- Brim 5 mm on the outer segments (tall and thin); none needed on the inner ones.
- **Elephant-foot compensation 0.** In vase mode it pulls the single line inward and narrows the socket mouth: 0.15 mm would leave 0.1 mm instead of 0.25 mm clearance around the rim below.
- Print the foot (socket) down, as exported.
- Normal (non-vase) mode works too with 1 wall and **Wall generator = Arachne**: the classic generator prints the wall as two overlapping 0.62 mm loops, about 1.5× the material and oversized.
- Tip: tick "Include fit test" in the download panel to get two short rings for checking the joint clearance (now 0.25 mm) before printing every segment.

### Base — normal mode

- Print top-up, as exported, and **keep it centred** on the bed: Bambu Studio's auto-arrange keeps a margin around parts with supports and refuses a 240 mm base on a 256 mm bed.
- 4 walls, 20 % gyroid infill, 5 top and 5 bottom layers, elephant-foot compensation 0.15 mm.
- **Tree supports, on build plate only**: the 158 mm plate pocket in the underside has a flat ceiling. The cable tunnel has a 45° teardrop roof and needs no support.

### Top cover — normal mode

- Print plate-down, as exported (rings and boss pointing up), no supports. The top edge is a 45° chamfer blending into a round, so nothing overhangs more than 45°.
- 3 walls, 20 % infill, 0.2 mm layers for a clean top surface, elephant-foot compensation 0.15 mm.

## Notes

- The 158 mm plate pocket ceiling needs tree supports (build plate only).
"
`;

